C125121  U_OPTO  ADJUDICATED-PAD-GEOM  SMDIP-4, and the delta POINTS THE WRONG WAY - re-measured 2026-07-26 on the v1.3 board. The twin compares pad1<->pad4 CENTRE span (ours 9.530 vs JLC 10.000, d0.470) but the property this land exists to hold is the CLEAR STRIP between the two lead rows, i.e. the LTV-817S input<->output isolation barrier (5000Vrms; 02_parts/LTV-817S-TA1/part.yaml: 'the wide-body SMDIP-4 (W9.53mm) land holds the two lead rows ~9.53mm apart - preserve that full creepage/clearance across the barrier'). MEASURED, footprint-local: OURS rows at x=+-4.765 with 2.00mm-wide pads -> inner edges +-3.765 -> CLEAR STRIP 7.530mm. JLC OPTO-SMD-4_L4.6-W6.5-P2.54-LS10.3-BL rows at y=+-5.000 with 3.00mm-tall pads -> inner edges +-3.500 -> CLEAR STRIP 7.000mm. So JLC separates the ROWS 0.470mm further and then spends 0.265mm per side reaching back toward the barrier, leaving its strip 0.530mm NARROWER than ours. Our land is the CONSERVATIVE one on the only axis that matters, and adopting JLC would ERODE the barrier. Domains split as designed: pads 1/2 = OPTO_LED_A/GND (SELV, -x), pads 3/4 = CONTACTOR_E/CONTACTOR_C (isolated, +x); the strip is additionally denied to tracks/vias/pours on all four layers by the floorplan `opto_barrier` keepout [181.4,85.8,188.6,94.2], and the copper either side is held at 2.0mm by the `opto_isolation_2mm` DRU rule. Pitch 2.54 identical, 4-pad topology matches, fit non-mirrored; render pin-1 dot matches pad 1. This adjudication blesses GEOMETRY only - C125121 also carries a MEASURED rotation row, and the ORDER_README human gate names U_OPTO first because a rotated opto swaps the LED and transistor sides ACROSS the barrier.
